This lets your bundler load only the JavaScript and CSS for the components you use:"},"15":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#per-component-imports","content":"This also works with autocomplete in IDEs and LLMs, so you can import from the root package and let your editor/agent suggest the available components."},"16":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#framework-setup","content":"Antares ships CSS alongside its JavaScript modules. Each component chunk imports a corresponding `.css` file (e.g., `import './src-BZhWcxqJ.css'`). Most bundlers handle this automatically, but some frameworks need extra configuration to process CSS imports from `node_modules`."},"17":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#nextjs","content":"Add `@godaddy/antares` to `transpilePackages` so Next.js processes the package through its own CSS pipeline instead of treating it as a pre-built external:"},"18":{"id":"/docs-16","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#nextjs","content":"Without this, Next.js will throw:"},"19":{"id":"/docs-17","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#remix","content":"Remix with Vite handles CSS imports from `node_modules` in the client bundle automatically. However, during SSR, Vite treats `node_modules` as externals by default, which bypasses CSS processing. Add `@godaddy/antares` to `ssr.noExternal` to fix this:"},"20":{"id":"/docs-18","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#vite","content":"Vite processes CSS imports from `node_modules` out of the box. No additional configuration is needed for client-side SPAs."},"21":{"id":"/docs-19","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#vite","content":"If you are using Vite with SSR (e.g., custom SSR setup, not Remix), add `@godaddy/antares` to `ssr.noExternal` as shown in the Remix section."},"22":{"id":"/docs-20","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#other-bundlers","content":"Any bundler that supports CSS imports will work with Antares. If your bundler does not process CSS imports from `node_modules` by default, ensure it is configured to do so. For example, with raw webpack you may need `css-loader` configured to handle `.css` files from `node_modules`."},"23":{"id":"/docs/components/alert","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"page","content":"Alert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert"},"24":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-0","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert","content":"In-page alerts are non-intrusive notifications within a webpage, providing users with timely information or feedback without disrupting their experience."},"25":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-1","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#installation","content":"Installation"},"26":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-2","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#examples","content":"Examples"},"27":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-3","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#default","content":"Default"},"28":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-4","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#emphasis-variants","content":"Emphasis Variants"},"29":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-5","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#dismissible","content":"Dismissible"},"30":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-6","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#with-action","content":"With Action"},"31":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-7","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"32":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-8","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"33":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-9","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#screen-readers","content":"Screen readers"},"34":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-10","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#dismiss-button-label","content":"Dismiss button label"},"35":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-11","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"36":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-12","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#props","content":"Props"},"37":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-13","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#alert","content":"Alert"},"38":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-14","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#default","content":"A minimal alert with a title and body text."},"39":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-15","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#emphasis-variants","content":"All 7 emphasis categories. Each variant carries a distinct visual accent and semantic icon so the type of message is never communicated by color alone."},"40":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-16","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#dismissible","content":"When an `onClose` callback is provided, a dismiss button is rendered. The component does not manage its own visibility — the parent is responsible for unmounting or hiding the alert when `onClose` fires."},"41":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-17","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#with-action","content":"Pass a `Button` to the `actions` slot to give the user a clear path to resolve the alert."},"42":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-18","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Key"},"43":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-19","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Description"},"44":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-20","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"45":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-21","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the dismiss button or action button"},"46":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-22","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"`Space` / `Enter`"},"47":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-23","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Activates the focused button"},"48":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-24","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#screen-readers","content":"The alert container uses `role=\"alert\"`, which creates an ARIA live region. When an alert is rendered or its content changes, screen readers announce the message automatically — the user does not need to navigate to the alert to hear it."},"49":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-25","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#dismiss-button-label","content":"The dismiss button defaults to `aria-label=\"Close\"`. Override it via `ariaLabels={{ close: '...' }}` to provide more specific context for screen readers (e.g. `\"Dismiss payment warning\"`). This is especially useful when multiple alerts are visible at the same time."},"50":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-26","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Write alert content from the user's perspective: describe what happened and what they can do next, not the underlying technical error."},"51":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-27","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Use `critical` only when the user truly cannot continue without resolving the issue. Overusing it reduces its impact."},"52":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-28","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Always provide a `title` when the alert includes a dismiss button — it improves the reading experience for screen reader users."},"53":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-29","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"When using `actions`, prefer `secondary` or `tertiary` Button variants. Avoid placing a primary action inside an alert."},"54":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-30","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Do not stack multiple alerts of the same emphasis; consolidate the message into a single alert."},"55":{"id":"/docs/components/button","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"page","content":"Button","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button"},"56":{"id":"/docs/components/button-0","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"The Button component allows users to initiate actions or submit forms with a single click"},"57":{"id":"/docs/components/button-1","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#installation","content":"Installation"},"58":{"id":"/docs/components/button-2","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#examples","content":"Examples"},"59":{"id":"/docs/components/button-3","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#default","content":"Default"},"60":{"id":"/docs/components/button-4","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#primary","content":"Primary"},"61":{"id":"/docs/components/button-5","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#secondary","content":"Secondary"},"62":{"id":"/docs/components/button-6","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#tertiary","content":"Tertiary"},"63":{"id":"/docs/components/button-7","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#critical","content":"Critical"},"64":{"id":"/docs/components/button-8","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"65":{"id":"/docs/components/button-9","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#icon","content":"Icon"},"66":{"id":"/docs/components/button-10","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#inline","content":"Inline"},"67":{"id":"/docs/components/button-11","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#minimal","content":"Minimal"},"68":{"id":"/docs/components/button-12","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"69":{"id":"/docs/components/button-13","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#props","content":"Props"},"70":{"id":"/docs/components/button-14","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#button","content":"Button"},"71":{"id":"/docs/components/button-15","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#linkbutton","content":"LinkButton"},"72":{"id":"/docs/components/button-16","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#closebutton","content":"CloseButton"},"73":{"id":"/docs/components/button-17","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Use the `LinkButton` component instead when you need navigation functionality with a button-like appearance."},"74":{"id":"/docs/components/button-18","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Use the `CloseButton` preset to dismiss an overlay (such as a `Modal`). It defaults to `slot=\"close\"`, so it picks up the overlay's close behavior with no wiring, and always renders an `x` icon with `aria-label=\"Close\"`. For a labelled dismiss action (e.g. \"Cancel\"), use a raw `<Button slot=\"close\">Cancel</Button>`."},"75":{"id":"/docs/components/button-19","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Inside a field `Group`, `slot=\"control\"` and `slot=\"trigger\"` pick up the matching look, size, and\ndisabled state from context. See TextField for control affixes, and Select or DatePicker for trigger faces.\nThe `control` and `trigger` variants are field parts: the field sizes them, so use them only inside a field."},"76":{"id":"/docs/components/button-20","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#default","content":"The default/tertiary button is the base for all other buttons in the system. It provides no significant visual treatment other than to provide indication for the user to take a common action."},"77":{"id":"/docs/components/button-21","page_id":"/docs/components/button","ta