components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Pass a `number[]` to render a range with two thumbs and step markers."},"1194":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For a single value, prefer a visible `label`; use `aria-label` only when equivalent visible context already exists."},"1195":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For an array, provide one descriptive `thumbLabels` entry for every value. Entries are matched by index, so keep them aligned when values are added, removed, or reordered. Describe each thumb's purpose, such as `Lower warning threshold`, rather than its current number."},"1196":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."},"1197":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Each thumb follows the React Aria slider keyboard model:"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Tab and Shift+Tab move among thumbs and surrounding controls."},"1199":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Right and Arrow Up increase the focused value by `step`."},"1200":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-44","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Left and Arrow Down decrease the focused value by `step`."},"1201":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-45","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Home and End move the focused thumb to its permitted bounds."},"1202":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-46","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Page Up and Page Down make larger changes."},"1203":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-47","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Directional behavior follows the user's locale where appropriate. Pointer, touch, and keyboard interaction all use the same scale and constraints."},"1204":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-48","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Markers are decorative and hidden from the accessibility tree. Ensure the field label, thumb labels, bounds, step, and formatted values communicate all required information without relying on marker appearance."},"1205":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-49","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use an array only when every entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."},"1206":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-50","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep `value`, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` aligned by index."},"1207":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-51","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use thumb labels that explain purpose instead of repeating the current number."},"1208":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-52","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep array values in a stable semantic order. If crossing or reordering thumbs would make their meaning ambiguous, enforce the appropriate ordering in product state."},"1209":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-53","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Avoid large value arrays. Every entry creates another focusable control, which increases keyboard effort and cognitive load."},"1210":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-54","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Set meaningful `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` values. The scale should match the precision users actually need."},"1211":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-55","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use markers only when there are few enough steps to scan. Tiny steps across a large range can create an excessive number of DOM elements."},"1212":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-56","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `formatOptions` for currency, percentages, measurements, and other locale-sensitive units so values display and announce their meaning."},"1213":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-57","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `description` for persistent guidance and `isRequired` when a value is required."},"1214":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-58","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value should remain visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1215":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-59","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `onChange` for lightweight immediate feedback and `onChangeEnd` for expensive requests, filtering, or calculations."},"1216":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-60","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."},"1217":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-61","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"Check the same index in `thumbLabels` and `thumbNames`. Each array entry renders a thumb, and its accessible label and form name are read from the corresponding positions. A form name does not replace an accessible label."},"1218":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-62","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"Keep the controlled or default value and callback signatures consistent. When inference is unavailable, provide the generic explicitly: `<RangeField<number>>` for a scalar or `<RangeField<number[]>>` for an array."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-63","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The `value` prop is the source of truth. Update the scalar or array in `onChange` without changing its intended shape. For arrays, return a new array so application state observes the update."},"1220":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-64","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Verify that `step` represents the intended interval from `minValue`. Every thumb snaps to valid positions on the same configured scale."},"1221":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-65","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"Markers begin at `minValue` and appear at complete step positions. `maxValue` receives a marker only when the range is evenly divisible by `step`."},"1222":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-66","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Increase `step` or omit `markers`. Large ranges with small steps can produce many decorative elements even when users cannot distinguish them visually."},"1223":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-67","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"Enable automatic current-value output with `valueLabel={true}` or provide custom content. `minLabel` and `maxLabel` display only explicitly supplied content; neither defaults to a numeric bound or receives `formatOptions`."},"1224":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-68","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values are supported. Set a negative `minValue` and ensure every scalar or array value remains within the configured bounds."},"1225":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-69","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"Provide finite bounds where `minValue` is less than `maxValue`, a finite `step` greater than zero, and finite values inside the configured range."},"1226":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"page","content":"Responsive","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive"},"1227":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-0","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive","content":"Shared viewport breakpoints, native CSS patterns, and a media-query hook for responsive behavior."},"1228":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-1","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#features","content":"Features"},"1229":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-2","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#examples","content":"Examples"},"1230":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-3","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#default","content":"Default"},"1231":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-4","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#breakpoints","content":"Breakpoints"},"1232":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-5","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#viewport-layout","content":"Viewport Layout"},"1233":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-6","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#container-layout","content":"Container Layout"},"1234":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-7","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#form","content":"Form"},"1235":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-8","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#customization","content":"Customization"},"1236":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-9","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#server-rendering","content":"Server rendering"},"1237":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-10","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1238":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-11","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/responsive#api","content":"API"},"1239":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-12","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#features","content":"Shared, mobile-first viewport widths and query strings."},"1240":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-13","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#features","content":"Native CSS media and container queries for styling."},"1241":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-14","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#features","content":"`useMediaQuery` for media-dependent React behavior, with an explicit server fallback."},"1242":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-15","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#default","content":"Resize the viewport across `lg` to see the query change. Use this hook for behavior that\nneeds JavaScript; ordinary responsive styles belong in CSS."},"1243":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-16","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#breakpoints","content":"Widths and inclusive minimum-width query strings come from the same definitions."},"1244":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-17","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#viewport-layout","content":"CSS changes this layout from one column to two at the shared `lg` viewport threshold.\nLeave `columns` unset so it does not place a competing value in inline styles."},"1245":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-18","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#container-layout","content":"The cards respond to their named container, independently of the viewport. The local\n30rem threshold belongs to this layout, not the shared viewport scale."},"1246":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-19","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#form","content":"Type into a field and resize across `lg`. CSS reflows the same inputs, preserving their\nvalues, focus, and selection. Let CSS own columns and allow long descriptions to wrap."},"1247":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-20","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#customization","content":"Exports are available from `@godaddy/antares` and `@godaddy/antares/Responsive`. Pass any valid\nmedia-query string to `useMediaQuery`, including device preferences such as reduced motion.\nViewport widths describe available space; each component chooses the thresholds it needs.\nIn media queries, `rem` uses the browser's initial font size."},"1248":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-21","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#customization","content":"The examples include their CSS in `<style>` blocks so the complete code is visible. Applications can\nplace those rules in their own stylesheets. Let responsive CSS own both the base and query values\nfor a property; leave its corresponding layout prop and inline `style` unset. Normal cascade rules\nstill apply. A named container controls its descendants; portaled content needs a suitable\ncontainer in its own DOM ancestry. A container can't take its width from its content, so give it one\nfrom its parent, as the container example does with `inline-size: 100%`. Otherwise it collapses in flex\nrows and other shrink-to-fit layouts."},"1249":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-22","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#server-rendering","content":"Use the same `ssrMatch` value on the server and client. It is returned on the server, during initial\nhydration, and when `matchMedia` is unavailable. After hydration the hook adopts the browser result;\nclient-only rendering uses it immediately. Changing the query replaces the subscription, and\nunmounting removes it."},"1250":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-23","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#accessibility","content":"Preserve reading order, keyboard focus, and entered values as layouts change. If a component swaps\nReact trees, it must manage state and focus across that transition. Validate its chosen behavior\nwith long text, RTL, narrow widths, text enlargement, and browser zoom. Resizing the viewport alone\ndoes not test every effect of zoom. Use pointer and hover media features to detect input capabilities."},"1251":{"id":"/docs/components/responsive-24","page_id":"/docs/components/responsive","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/responsive#api","content":"Breakpoint values are listed in the Breakpoints example above. Types: `ViewportBreakpoint` and `UseMediaQueryOptions`."},"1252":{"id":"/docs/components/select","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"page","content":"Select","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select"},"1253":{"id":"/docs/components/select-0","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select","content":"Select is a dropdown for picking one or more values from a list of options. It renders a labeled trigger and a popover listbox, supports single and multiple selection, and submits naturally inside a form."},"1254":{"id":"/docs/components/select-1","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"Features"},"1255":{"id":"/docs/components/select-2","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#installation","content":"Installation"},"1256":{"id":"/docs/components/select-3","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#examples","content":"Examples"},"1257":{"id":"/docs/components/select-4","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#default","content":"Default"},"1258":{"id":"/docs/components/select-5","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1259":{"id":"/docs/components/select-6","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#multiple","content":"Multiple"},"1260":{"id":"/docs/components/select-7","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#invalid","content":"Invalid"},"1261":{"id":"/docs/components/select-8","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"1262":{"id":"/docs/components/select-9","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#form","content":"Form"},"1263":{"id":"/docs/components/select-10","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1264":{"id":"/docs/components/select-11","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#composed","content":"Composed"},"1265":{"id":"/docs/components/select-12","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#props","content":"Props"},"1266":{"id":"/docs/components/select-13","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#select","content":"Select"},"1267":{"id":"/docs/components/select-14","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectoptions","content":"SelectOptions"},"1268":{"id":"/docs/components/select-15","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectvalue","content":"SelectValue"},"1269":{"id":"/docs/components/select-16","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectitem","content":"SelectItem"},"1270":{"id":"/docs/components/select-17","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, a `Button slot=\"trigger\"`, `SelectOptions`, and optional `Text` / `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in"},"1271":{"id":"/docs/components/select-18","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"},"1272":{"id":"/docs/components/select-19","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Composed in another field**: Use `variant=\"control\"` to sit inside another field's `Group`, as a country-code select beside a phone `Input`"},"1273":{"id":"/docs/components/select-20","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values"},"1274":{"id":"/docs/components/select-21","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"},"1275":{"id":"/docs/components/select-22","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"},"1276":{"id":"/docs/components/select-23","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets the label, trigger, and options, which open at the same size even though they render in a portal. Without it, the Select follows the surrounding scope"},"1277":{"id":"/docs/components/select-24","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Form integration**: Set `name` and the value submits as part of a native `<form>` (multiple values submit as repeated entries)"},"1278":{"id":"/docs/components/select-25","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**React Aria integration**: Built on React Aria Select for accessibility, keyboard navigation, and typeahead"},"1279":{"id":"/docs/components/select-26","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#default","content":"Minimal usage with a `Label`, items, and a placeholder."},"1280":{"id":"/docs/components/select-27","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state."},"1281":{"id":"/docs/components/select-28","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#multiple","content":"Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values. `value` is an array of keys."},"1282":{"id":"/docs/components/select-29","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#invalid","content":"Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` for validation feedback."},"1283":{"id":"/docs/components/select-30","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` to prevent interaction."},"1284":{"id":"/docs/components/select-31","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#form","content":"Set `name` to submit the value with a native `<form>`. Multiple-mode values submit as repeated entries with the same `name`."},"1285":{"id":"/docs/components/select-32","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#sizes","content":"Compare the supported `md` and `sm` visual sizes."},"1286":{"id":"/docs/components/select-33","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#composed","content":"Write the trigger and the overlay yourself instead of composing `SelectOptions`, for full control\nover the popover and the list."},"1287":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"page","content":"SegmentedController","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller"},"1288":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-0","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","content":"A segmented controller is a linear set of two or more segments, each of which functions as a button. A segmented controller allows users to select options, switch views, or sort elements."},"1289":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-1","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#installation","content":"Installation"},"1290":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-2","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#examples","content":"Examples"},"1291":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-3","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"Default"},"1292":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-4","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1293":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-5","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1294":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-6","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Icon + Text"},"1295":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-7","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"Icon Only"},"1296":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-8","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","cont